   ❌ kit check finds 2 differences from the release → 🔧 setup

   kit keeps a repository trustworthy while people and agents work in it side by side.

   What kit is

   kit is your house rules as a versioned release, and the checks that hold the work to them. It places the rules where
   people and agents both look: .kit/1st.md, which every agent reads first, a rule for each kind of file, and the files
   each agent harness reads. Its commands do what the rules describe, so the right way is also the short way. Take a
   new release, and the rules and checks move with it, in every repository that takes it.

